.TH "FLOX\-UNINSTALL" "1" "" "" "Flox User Manuals"
.SH NAME
flox\-uninstall \- remove packages from an environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
flox [<general options>] (uninstall|rm)
     [\-d=<path> | \-r=<owner/name>]
     <packages>
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Uninstall packages from an environment.
.PP
Just like package installation, package uninstallation is transactional.
See \f[B]\f[CB]flox\-install(1)\f[B]\f[R] for more details on
transactions.
Requesting to uninstall multiple packages where at least one of them was
not previously installed will cause the transaction to fail and no
packages will be uninstalled.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Remove Options
.TP
\f[CR]<packages>\f[R]
The install IDs or package paths of the packages to remove.
If the manifest contains both an install ID and a package with matching
package path, the install ID takes precedence.
If the same package path is installed under different install IDs, an
error is returned.
A package path can optionally contain the original version constraint.
.SS Environment Options
If no environment is specified for an environment command, the
environment in the current directory or the active environment that was
last activated is used.
.TP
\f[CR]\-d\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-dir\f[R]
Path containing a .flox/ directory.
.TP
\f[CR]\-r\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-reference\f[R]
A FloxHub environment, specified in the form \f[CR]<owner>/<name>\f[R].
.TP
\f[CR]\-D\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-default\f[R]
Use your default environment (\f[CR]<your\-user>/default\f[R]).
When unauthenticated in an interactive context, you will be prompted to
log in.
In non\-interactive contexts (e.g., scripts or CI), this flag will fail
with an error when authentication is missing.
.SS General Options
.TP
\f[CR]\-h\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-help\f[R]
Prints help information.
.PP
The following options can be passed when running any \f[CR]flox\f[R]
subcommand but must be specified \f[I]before\f[R] the subcommand.
.TP
\f[CR]\-v\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-verbose\f[R]
Increase logging verbosity.
Invoke multiple times for increasing detail.
.TP
\f[CR]\-q\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-quiet\f[R]
Silence logs except for errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
